   "text": "This structure is SN-38 (7-ethyl-10-hydroxycamptothecin), read from the drawing as follows.\n\n- **Core:** a camptothecin-type pentacyclic skeleton. It has a quinoline unit fused to a five-membered ring containing N, then a pyridone, then a lactone.\n- **Substituents:** an ethyl group on the quinoline carbon next to the ring fusion, and an OH on the benzo ring, separated from the ring-fusion carbon by one CH.\n- **Quaternary carbon:** it carries an ethyl group, a hashed OH, the lactone C=O and the ring carbon.\n\nFor the stereocentre, I assigned CIP priorities as OH > lactone C(=O)O > ring carbon > ethyl. With the OH hashed (pointing back) and the ethyl in the plane, this gives the S configuration, which matches natural camptothecin. In the SMILES the neighbour order at that carbon is lactone C, ring-closure carbon, OH, ethyl, and `[C@]` encodes S for that order.\n\nSMILES: CCC1=C2CN3C(=CC4=C(C3=O)COC(=O)[C@]4(O)CC)C2=NC2=CC=C(O)C=C12"
